      <description>Chinese President Xi Jinping has touched down in Washington, marking three years since he last visited the US. His much-anticipated one-day summit with President Donald Trump on Sept. 24 will offer the leaders of the world’s two largest economies a chance to improve personal ties and look for common ground on contentious topics including trade, artificial intelligence, the Iran war and the future of Taiwan.</description>
